# Vendored: gtkwave/libfst

- Source: https://github.com/gtkwave/libfst
- Commit: c716c1f67e21a06aaf8722830b371516e70dc657 (branch `main`)
- License: MIT (Tony Bybell), see `LICENSE` — compatible with wolvicmod's MIT.

## Files taken

- `src/fstapi.c`, `src/fstapi.h` — FST reader/writer API
- `src/fastlz.c`, `src/fastlz.h`, `src/lz4.c`, `src/lz4.h` — compression used by the writer
- `src/fst_win_unistd.h` — Windows compatibility (unused on Linux)
- `doc/block_format.txt` — FST block format reference

Upstream's `tests/` and meson build files are not taken; building is handled by
`CMakeLists.txt` in this directory.

## Build notes

- Compiled without `FST_INCLUDE_CONFIG`: no `config.h` is needed on Linux when
  building with `-D_GNU_SOURCE` (`fseeko`/`realpath` are available).
- `FST_WRITER_PARALLEL` auto-disables without `HAVE_LIBPTHREAD`: no pthread
  dependency (single-threaded writer).
- bzip2 is not used by `fstapi.c` (upstream meson links it for other tools).
- Only external dependency: zlib (`find_package(ZLIB)`).
